Field OverviewWhat this patent landscape coversMatrix LED and pixel-light headlight systems replace fixed-beam optics with arrays of individually addressable light segments, allowing a headlamp to reshape its beam pattern in real time to avoid glare while keeping high-beam illumination on the rest of the road. This landscape covers 116 published records filed or published between 2015 and the 2026 data cut-off, matched on claims and abstracts referencing matrix LED, matrix headlight or pixel light hardware combined with beam pattern, glare or shaping functions in a vehicle or headlamp context. Patent families are the unit that matters most here, since a single beam-shaping concept is often filed in parallel across the US, China, EPO, Germany, WIPO and the UK.The assignee ranking returned by the data endpoint lists 50 companies, spanning established headlamp tier-one suppliers, several major automakers, and a long tail of single or few-filing entrants. Filing activity by receiving office shows the United States and China as the two largest venues, with Europe, Germany, WIPO and the UK trailing behind — a pattern consistent with a technology still being contested across multiple regional markets rather than settled in one jurisdiction.Filing activity and IPC composition, 2015–20261MAY PATENTS LTD7See their portfolio2SNAP AID PATENTS LTD7See their portfolio3MERCEDES BENZ GROUP AG7See their portfolio4VALEO VISION SA7See their portfolio5GM GLOBAL TECHNOLOGY OPERATIONS LLC6See their portfolio6KOITO MFG CO LTD6See their portfolio7AUTOSYSTEMS BELLEVILLE INC6See their portfolio8KIA CORPORATION4See their portfolio9ZKW GRP GMBH4See their portfolio10HYUNDAI MOTOR CO LTD4See their portfolio11HASCO VISION TECHNOLOGY CO LTD3See their portfolio12JAGUAR LAND ROVER LTD3See their portfolio13SWISS REINSURANCE CO LTD3See their portfolio14DR ING H C F PORSCHE AG3See their portfolio15AUDI AG3See their portfolio16NNG SOFTWARE DEVING & COMML LLC3See their portfolio17CHANGZHOU XINGYU AUTOMOT